  "data_abstract": "The first relative transverse momentum ($k_{\\text{T}}$) scan of the Lund jet plane of high-energy jets produced in lead-lead (PbPb) collisions is presented and compared to the result obtained in proton-proton (pp) collisions. The PbPb (pp) data were recorded by the CMS experiment in 2018 (2017) and correspond to an integrated luminosity of $1.7$ nb$^{-1}$ ($301$ pb$^{-1}$) at a nucleon-nucleon center-of-mass energy of 5.02 TeV. The angular distribution of the primary emissions with the highest $k_{\\text{T}}$ of anti-$k_{\\text{T}}$ jets with a distance parameter $R=0.4$ is reported. Two different ranges of $k_{\\text{T}}$ are investigated for jets with transverse momentum in the range $200 < p_{\\text{T}}^\\text{jet} < 1000$ GeV, in order to explore the energy scale dependence of the jet quenching phenomena.The measurement was designed to test whether the earliest jet emissions are produced before the formation of the quark-gluon plasma in PbPb collisions.The angular distribution of emissions at high $k_{\\text{T}}$ has a similar shape in pp and PbPb collisions, which is consistent with the emissions being part of the early and vacuum-like regime of the jet evolution in PbPb collisions.",
